<%#
  views/partials/head.ejs

  The head element shared by every page: character set, the viewport for phones, the
  page title and the one shared stylesheet.

  Locals (both optional):
    title       - the page title shown in the browser tab and in search results.
                  Default: the site name.
    description - a one-sentence summary for search engines (the article page passes the
                  article's summary). Left out when not given.
  "locals.title" instead of "title": reading a local that a page didn't pass would make
  EJS throw, while reading it from locals just gives undefined.

  The viewport meta tag makes phones use the real screen width instead of pretending to be
  a desktop, which is what makes the responsive CSS work (requirements: computer, tablet
  and phone). Express serves the public folder at "/" (app.js), so public/css/main.css is
  at /css/main.css.

  Included by: every page view.
  Owner: SH.
%>
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title><%= locals.title || 'The Daily Web' %></title>
    <% if (locals.description) { %>
    <meta name="description" content="<%= locals.description %>">
    <% } %>
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="/css/main.css">
</head>
